ic","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T19:28:57Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T19:28:57Z","body":"It has been long enough, I should clarify what my goals for this PR are.\r\n\r\nThis PR implements a mechanism for arbitrary windows to be restored if they are assigned a `session_id`. *As an example of this,* the QuickSettings and QuickOpen windows have `session_id`s which means they will be restored. If you want to suggest for this PR to restore more windows than this, please clarify that you want to expand the purpose of this PR (I read \"SceneTreeDialog cannot restore position and size.\" as \"I expected SceneTreeDialog to be restored but it wasn't which seems like a bug\"). As for the things about remembering more information, `set_window_metadata` is technically extremely generic. I could expose this method to scripting to attach additional metadata beyond what windows intrinsically store (like having QuickOpen manage its own grid/list toggle state) but I don't want to add too much logic exclusive to QuickOpen.\r\n\r\nAs for the popups, certainly the parameter shouldn't just be ignored. However, if the project setting is enabled, presumably the developer is expecting windows to be restored and overriding the default popup location with a saved location already has precedent in godot like the code you mentioned.\r\n\r\n> Maybe can refer to\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/aac131f3865a712ea2274921618be3e9f790da1a/editor/gui/create_dialog.cpp#L70-L73\r\n> \r\n> This implements restoring the size and position of the create_new_node dialog.\r\n\r\nI don't see a reason to split window restoration into a project setting for the developer's project and an editor setting for the editor itself but maybe there's an argument for this that I missed?\r\n\r\nIt's still going to take me a bit more to actually get round to optimising `popup` calls to noops if the window is going to be restored anyway but I believe that overring the paramter makes sense here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4113169068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4115242170","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106648#issuecomment-4115242170","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106648","id":4115242170,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71SZy6","user":{"login":"actforjason","id":57058325,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MDU4MzI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57058325?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason","html_url":"https://github.com/actforjason","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-24T04:01:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T12:39:28Z","body":">  (like having QuickOpen manage its own grid/list toggle state) \r\n\r\nI haven't noticed these at first:\r\nGrid/List toggle state can be restored by setting `Last Used` at `filesystem/quick_open_dialog/default_display_mode`. There are other relative settings at `filesystem/quick_open_dialog/`\r\n\r\n> However, if the project setting is enabled, presumably the developer is expecting windows to be restored and overriding the default popup location with a saved location already has precedent in godot like the code you mentioned.\r\n\r\nAs this code shows, it determines and passes cached data before popups. But absolutely there are too many dialogs, and it is hard to write and read the cache separately. \r\n\r\nFurthermore just like CreateDialog, restoration as default, no need to set the option.\r\n\r\n> I don't see a reason to split window restoration into a project setting for the developer's project and an editor setting for the editor itself but maybe there's an argument for this that I missed?\r\n\r\nFor games, isn't it possible to restore window using the set/get methods of the Window's [position](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_window.html#class-window-property-position) and [size](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_window.html#class-window-property-size) controlled by `visibility_changed` and `visible`, without an additional session_id?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4115242170/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4134689136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106648#issuecomment-4134689136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106648","id":4134689136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72cllw","user":{"login":"actforjason","id":57058325,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MDU4MzI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57058325?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason","html_url":"https://github.com/actforjason","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/actforjason/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T13:16:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T13:20:28Z","body":"Now it only works for QuickOpenDialog, but there are more than 50 derived classes of AcceptDialog and ConfirmationDialog, many of these require the restoration of bounds. According to the current method, need to configure them one by one in pr.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4134689136/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4226168515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106648#issuecomment-4226168515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106648","id":4226168515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc775jbD","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-10T19:17:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-10T19:17:00Z","body":"Hi, sorry for the delay and thank you for looking into this!\r\n\r\nI think that the general approach is good, although I would prefer something simpler. Please TIWAGOS as I've only taken a cursory look for now. Sorry about anything I might have missed.\r\n\r\nPersonally I'd keep the API to the bare minimum and disable all sort of fancy features, at least to begin with. The leaner, the less controversial and the faster this gets in. We also have less chances to mess the API and need to deprecate/no-op something in the long run.\r\n\r\nRoughly speaking, I think that windows could just have a \"restore name\" and have manual, explicit, abstract \"restore/save\" semantics, without direct metadata access or automatic restoring.\r\n\r\nThis would allow the implementation to do anything it pleases without exposing _too much_ interface to the user. I think that our initial requirement is to have a \"system offloadable\" replacement for the editor window restore API, as it's already an actively used internal implementation of this feature. \r\n\r\nWe could thus have a default \"userspace\" implementation in e.g. `Window`, while still allowing to call the platform specific API (through e.g. a feature flag check).\r\n\r\nAs a last note, I'm afraid that the current revision of this PR might not mesh well with the wayland session restore API. It only exposes a generic [`restore_toplevel`](https://wayland.app/protocols/xx-session-management-v1#xx_session_v1:request:restore_toplevel) request and, for whatever reason, [only allows restoring the window before mapping](https://wayland.app/protocols/xx-session-management-v1#xx_session_v1:request:restore_toplevel:~:text=This%20request%20must%20be%20called%20prior%20to%20the%20first%20commit%20on%20the%20associated%20wl%5Fsurface%2C%20otherwise%20an%20already%5Fmapped%20error%20is%20raised). We definitely need to take these caveats into consideration.\r\n\r\nIn summary I think that the feature is great! It will improve QoL for both users and application developers while exposing a feature that, more or less, is already there (internally). We just need to make sure that the API checks all the marks.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4226168515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]